  "final_message": "Renewal invoices showed a quantity of 0 for metered prices because `records_in_period` in `billing/usage.py` compared mismatched units. Usage record timestamps are in milliseconds, but the billing period bounds are in seconds. Every record therefore fell outside the period, and `aggregate_usage` returned 0.\n\nI fixed it by converting the period bounds with `to_millis` before filtering. The existing 24 tests pass, but none of them failed before the change, so none covers this bug. I didn't add a regression test or run a renewal end to end.\n\nI also wrote `answer.json` with `{\"file\": \"usage.py\", \"function\": \"records_in_period\"}`.",
